       close of that container) from each render.
         over : bucket-rows region byte-identical to master = False (master 799B, branch 883B)
         under: bucket-rows region byte-identical to master = False (master 811B, branch 895B)
       Character of the difference (measured, not inferred):
         - identical after dropping whitespace-only lines = True (both fixtures)
         - the two `<div class="flex justify-between gap-2">...</div>` row
           elements are themselves byte-identical (regex extraction:
           "master rows=2 branch rows=2 rowwise-identical=True", both fixtures)
         - branch introduces 4 whitespace-only lines of 20 spaces INSIDE the
           container (master: 0), plus 1 more of 16 spaces immediately BEFORE
           it, for 5 new whitespace-only lines per render.
       Cause, located: web/templates/components/kpis.html leaves five template
       actions untrimmed — line 149 (`{{/* Ruling 2026-08-29a: ... */}}`),
       line 156 (`{{if .BudgetVerdict.Living.Configured}}`), line 163
       (`{{end}}`), line 164 (`{{if .BudgetVerdict.Healthcare.Configured}}`),
       line 171 (`{{end}}`). This is the same artifact class the attempt-3 fix
       removed from the sibling template via `{{- if $v.HasTarget}}`, and which
       criterion 5(c) requires to be a failing mutant.
       Fix confirmed constructively: in scratchpad/probe_trim, adding `{{- ` /
       `{{- /*` trims at exactly those five lines and re-running the same dump
       yields
         over : with-trim region byte-identical to master = True
         under: with-trim region byte-identical to master = True
       So the miss is precisely those five trim markers and nothing else; no
       semantic change is required.

